  "articleBody": "Thinking about framing a new door opening yourself? That's awesome, but sometimes it’s really smart to bring in a professional. The biggest signal is if you suspect the wall you’re planning to alter is load-bearing. Messing with a load-bearing wall without the right knowledge can compromise your home’s structural integrity, and that’s a headache you definitely don’t want. Another big one is if you’re installing an expensive prehung door unit. These often require a super precise rough opening to operate correctly and look their best. If the opening isn't perfect, you could end up with a door that sticks, gaps, or doesn't close right, and nobody wants that. Also, if you're not confident in your ability to get the opening perfectly plumb, level, and square – which is crucial for proper door function – it’s a good idea to get some help. Even a slight error can lead to big alignment issues down the line. We specialize in custom framing and can handle anything from simple interior doors to complex load-bearing wall alterations. Give us a call at 303-505-0866 if you're unsure; we're happy to chat through your project.",
